## Key wake, both proven on battery (guardian-20261117-134252, read over Wi-Fi TUNE sessions)
- FRONT: wake_key=front reset=deepsleep wake_cause=ext1 (sleep_count 1 and 2).
- SIDE (the big side button, GPIO12): wake_key=side reset=deepsleep wake_cause=ext1 asleep_s=1436 sleep_count=3
  asleep_total_s=1643, battery 3797 mV / 62 %. Logs: sticks3-G16D-tune-wifi-session*.log and the 16:0x session.
- FINDING: sleep_faults=0x20 (FaultCodec) on all three sleeps: the ES8311 low-power writes at 0x18 fail. Cause not
  established: our firmware never initializes the codec (the ai-usage lineage does, through M5Unified, and does not
  check its write results), and the writes run after the LCD rail (PM1 GPIO2) is cut.
  FIX (test-first, idle_check): teardown probes 0x18 (address only) before writing; no ACK = InfoCodecUnpowered
  (0x100, information, no write), ACK + refused writes = FaultCodec. STATUS: sleep_faults masks information bits,
  sleep_codec=powered_down|unpowered|failed|-, codec_boot=ack|nack (probe with the rail on, before the IMU task).
  Host 45/45 plain+ASan, tools 35, bs 28, lab 93.
- guardian-20261117-153121 on device (OTA 15:3x): codec_boot=ack (ES8311 answers with the LCD rail on). After a deep sleep
  (short test timers power.dim_s=5 / power.sleep_s=10, restored to 30/120 in the same read, TUNE 1.7):
  reset=deepsleep wake_key=front asleep_s=432 sleep_codec=failed sleep_faults=0x20 -> the codec still ANSWERS its address
  after the rail cut (so the rail does not power it down) but refuses the power-down writes: it likely stays powered
  through deep sleep (the owner measured this class of leak). Cause of the refused writes: not established.
  NEXT FIX (test-first; the Guardian has no audio path: no I2S/speaker code): power the ES8311 down at BOOT with the
  same shared sequence (idle.hpp es8311_power_down), reporting codec_boot=down | nack | write_err:<esp_err>@<reg>.
- guardian-20261117-154925 on device: codec_boot=down (all three ES8311 power-down writes accepted at boot) while the
  sleep before it (same firmware) reported sleep_codec=failed. => the writes fail only inside the sleep sequence, which
  cut the LCD rail (PM1 GPIO2) before them. FIX (test-first, idle_check order case): I2C power-downs (BMI270, ES8311)
  run before display sleep and every rail cut. Measurement pending (one sleep). TUNE power.* left at 5/10 s for that
  check; restore to 30/120 in the same read.
- guardian-20261117-155649 on device (OTA ~16:00): after one deep sleep (asleep_s=151, wake_key=front):
  sleep_faults=0x0 sleep_codec=powered_down codec_boot=down. CONFIRMED: the ES8311 refused writes only after the LCD
