## Coverage hysteresis (owner: deauth flood made the "listening coverage degraded" line flap)
ROOT CAUSE (measured, live log): under a deauth flood the 24-slot radio queue overflows (rx_queue_full 1324->1391)
and the channel lock drops on 5 s silences, so each 1 s coverage window sees dropped_in_window>0 then 0, swinging
Coverage Fresh<->Degraded (degraded_transitions 35->38). The red ALERT held steady (0 flips); only the overlay LINE
flapped. The alert still fired and cleared cleanly (alert 1 through the ~45 s cooldown, then 0, face back to rating).
FIX (test-first, core_check, guardian_core Core): coverage uses one-directional hysteresis - a bad window (channel 0,
dropped_in_window>0, or a live core without passive receive) warns at once, but degraded clears only after coverage is
clean for Core::coverage_recover_ms (3 s). Brief clean windows inside a storm no longer flip it back; a real sustained
loss (AP gone) still degrades then goes stale/no-data via the existing age path. The honest grade stays blanked while
degraded, and the "coverage degraded" overlay still shows (intended signal), just steady now. 2 core tests added/updated,
1 condition test advanced past the hold. Host 45/45 plain+ASan, tools 36, bs 28, lab 93, 0 warnings.
NOTE: rx_queue_full under flood left as-is (honest; detection survived - you only need enough deauth to alert).

