## Face motion REWRITTEN (owner: "ITS COMPLETELY OFF, HORRIBLE, DITCH THIS APPROACH/CODE", "DOESN'T TILT", "WHITE STRAPS",
## then "SPIN... TILT WITH... REACT IN A FLUID WAY... 3 AXIS... CHECK MANUAL... STUDY STICKS3-TETRIS")
Backup before deletion (no git): backups/guardian-pre-motion-removal-20261117-180748.tgz sha256 82177c84...cf58 (the store, read back).
The pull-back/strong-defaults build (guardian-20261117-175405) was never installed (OTA server stopped, 0 /image).
ROOT CAUSES found in the old G16C model (why "doesn't tilt"): (1) "calm" (slow rotation) forced the targets to 0, so a tilt
HELD still showed nothing; (2) a "rest reference" slowly adopted the held pose; (3) screens.cpp applied motion only while
!calm. WHITE STRAPS: every accel spike >0.45 g was a "tap" that flashed all HUD rules + the level line WHITE.
NEW MODEL (from the owner's Stackfall, proven on this board: absolute held angle from gravity; axes per StickS3 manual p.6-7
and Stackfall imu_axes.h, matching our map 2,-1,3): complementary filter (gyro rotates "up", accel corrects with tau 0.3 s,
jolts down-weighted by |acc|-1g), three held axes: roll -> face spins WITH the stick (gain 1, bound 20 deg), pitch -> nod
(0.35 px/deg, 10 px), yaw (gyro about the vertical) -> turn (0.5 px/deg, 12 px, eases back 1.5 s); critically damped follower
3 Hz; pull_back 0.10 at the bounds; absolute up from the calibration (no rest adaptation, no calm reset, no tap flash).
Tests: motion_check rewritten (13 cases incl. a_held_roll_spins_the_face_with_the_stick_and_stays: 15 deg held 10 s);
companion_check: centred pose == still frame, no white HUD rule. Board: motion.* keys replaced; motion.rest_gyro/rest_acc
kept for G16D handling detection; STATUS motion=following|waiting, pose=roll,pitch,yaw.
